WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.629
COUNT can answer different questions so it is
important to choose the

00:00:03.655 --> 00:00:09.359
right version COUNT star counts input rows It does

00:00:09.372 --> 00:00:14.895
not care whether individual columns contain missing
values COUNT of a

00:00:14.908 --> 00:00:20.538
specific column counts only rows where that
expression is not NULL COUNT

00:00:20.551 --> 00:00:26.127
DISTINCT counts unique non-null values Now run the
example in

00:00:26.153 --> 00:00:31.669
the browser Compare the three result columns The
total admission

00:00:31.695 --> 00:00:36.905
count should include every admission row The
completed-admission count should be smaller

00:00:36.932 --> 00:00:42.353
because ongoing admissions have no discharge time
The distinct patient count answers

00:00:42.379 --> 00:00:47.881
a different question again how many unique patients
appear If you

00:00:47.907 --> 00:00:51.565
are using pgAdmin copy the query into the Query Tool
and run

00:00:51.591 --> 00:00:56.120
the same comparison there Look at the labels
carefully and connect each

00:00:56.147 --> 00:00:57.844
number to the question it answers
